From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:42:20 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/79] runner: the in-thinking runner core on the lane host,
 with a family binding

Fourth slice of the in-thinking runner port, from the DSV41
release branch (7b79ef92d). While a reply thinks, the engine watches committed
tokens for a closed code cell or an inline `<expr> =`, runs it on the circuit
or graph bank off the engine thread, and feeds the result tokens as owned rows
through the ordinary verify windows: no stop, no tool call, no re-render.

- runner.zig, runner_scan*.zig (fence, repl, inline and trace forms; the TeX
  and worded-operator abstention), runner_trace*.zig, runner_receipt.zig,
  runner_abstain.zig, runner_commit.zig (answer-commit, off unless set),
  runner_output.zig, runner_open.zig (circuit, bank and frontend at boot),
  runner_probe.zig, and their tests, the proof tests and the host benches.
- Lane glue: lanes/runner_hook.zig and runner_eos.zig, lane_host_runner.zig;
  Stream.runner / awaiting / settle and hold.resumeAwaiting / settle; the lane
  host ticks sessions and sends Event.cells and the finished reply's receipt;
  Request.run_cells / run_trace / run_commit and Info.runner in engine_api.
  The lanes test fake gains a scripted target.
- runner_binding.zig: a family's Binding is the generic TF_RUNNER prefix and
  an optional alias. DeepSeek-V4.1 reads TF_RUNNER* or TF_DSV41_RUNNER* as
  before; Flash-Next is a stub on the generic names its engine does not read
  yet. The prefix is chosen by its switch alone, because TF_RUNNER_CIRCUIT,
  _CLANG and _LLD also name tools for tests and image checks; both switches
  set is BadKnob. Config remembers its prefix, so a DSV41 boot's messages are
  unchanged, and the image boot check fails closed under either switch.

Nothing turns the runner on yet: no family opens it and no request sets
run_cells until the server and family bindings (next slice). The mailbox
ignores Event.cells until then. Build: test-runner-host,
test-runner-abstain-host, test-runner-proof-host (sharded, TF_RUNNER_CIRCUIT),
bench-runner-cost, bench-runner-hold, runner-frontend-check,
runner-link-check. Deferred: forced drafts past a forced tail, the round
trace and their fire tests (shared scheduling, a slice of their own); S3.
